        "title": "Stitch-to-review registration \u2022 export contract v1",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The tour window uses the ORIGINAL panorama grid: heading is panorama yaw, increasing to the right from the stitched left edge (0\u00b0). Elevation is panorama latitude, positive up. 360\u00b0 and 0\u00b0 are the same ray. The window is a perspective view, not a cropped flat sheet.",
          "Review azimuth is a compass angle in degrees, positive clockwise from north. North is located at northAtPanoramaYaw in the original panorama. panoramaYawDirection says whether increasing panorama yaw runs clockwise or counterclockwise around the compass. A counterclockwise export is a mirrored stitch, not a reversed compass.",
          "Review elevation is in degrees from the horizon. reviewElevationDirection is the capture recorder setting: up means positive above the horizon; down means positive below it. The panorama itself always has positive latitude up. There is no roll or other calibration offset.",
          "To register a review, start at the marked north yaw and advance the review azimuth with the stated direction. Reverse a down-positive elevation. Reduce yaw modulo 360\u00b0. Editing a hotspot reverses that same mapping; save compass azimuth in [0\u00b0,360\u00b0) and recorder elevation, not window pixels.",
          "A tap in Move hotspot mode replaces the one review position for this scene. Save review stores its position and label independently. Changing the window, crossing the seam or reopening a tour must not move it on the original scene. Original panoramas and capture records are read-only imports. Label edits do not change position."
        ],
        "fieldLabels": {
